\begin{equation} 
\mathscr{E}_M := \Bigl\{(Q, Q') \in \mathscr{D}_T \times \mathscr{D}_T : \exists \mathtt Q \in \mathscr{D}_M \text{ such that } Q, Q' \subseteq \mathtt Q \Bigr\}.
\end{equation}
Recall that $\mathscr{D}_M$ denotes all the dyadic descendants $\mathtt Q$ of $[0,1]^d$ of generation $M$; $\ell(\mathtt Q) = 2^{-M}$. Thus $\mathscr{E}_M$ consists of all pairs $(Q, Q') \in \mathscr{D}_T \times \mathscr{D}_T$ with the property that $Q,Q'$ have a common ancestor at generation $M$. 
